Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:58:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 3, patch 16 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M14;
 Review 80, a reader's finding F6, its second part, WHICH MAIN HAS NOT
 CHECKED: it was made again before it was mended): B1891'S LOCK COMPARES THE
 SET OF ROWS OF THE STATUS TABLES, AND REPORTS A ROW THAT ITS BUILDER DOES NOT
 READ.

THE FINDING, MADE AGAIN on the lock. It holds that no status cell of the foundation changed from version 1.65. It compared the cells of the rows the snapshot holds, and the set of rows that open with an identifier. It did not compare the set of rows of the status tables, so a row added to one was not seen. And the snapshot's builder reads a row by its bars with a space on each side: a row written with no spaces is read by neither of its two readings.

WHAT IS CHANGED. A new test compares both sets of rows with the snapshot, in both directions, and reports every table row of the foundation that has not as many cells as its table's header, counted as the builder counts them. On the foundation as it is: nothing differs, and no row goes unread. The builder, which is another arc's, is not changed.

THE PLANTED CASES, in the patch's own test: a row with no identifier added to a status table; a row with an identifier written with no spaces at its bars; a row with neither. Each passes the comparisons of the older test and is reported now. What the older test does see, a changed cell, is seen by both.

The lock: 5 tests pass. 0 of 19.
